# RChess Server — Deployment Guide

## Quick Start (Local LAN Game)

```bash
# Build
cargo build --release

# Run server (auto-detects your LAN IP for invite links)
./target/release/rchess-server

# Client connects to your LAN IP
./target/release/rchess
# → Online → Create Room → share the rc1:… invite link with your friend
# Friend: → Online → Join → paste the rc1:… link
```

---

## How Invite Links Work

When you create a room, the server generates an **invite link**:

```
rc1:bG9jYWxob3N0OjkwMDE6QUJDREVG
```

This is `rc1:` + base64url of `host:port:ROOMCODE`.

Your friend pastes this into rchess → Online → Join (instead of typing a code).
The TUI auto-decodes the host, port, and room code and connects directly.

**No manual IP typing needed.**

