## Deployment Options

### Option 1: Local (same machine / LAN)

```bash
./rchess-server
# Server auto-detects LAN IP, puts it in invite links
# Works immediately — share rc1:… link via chat/text
```

### Option 2: VPS / Cloud (public internet)

```bash
# With your domain or public IP
./rchess-server --public chess.example.com --port 9001

# Or in config file:
echo 'public_host = "chess.example.com"' >> ~/.config/rchess/server.toml
```

Friends anywhere in the world paste the `rc1:…` link.

### Option 3: Docker

```bash
# Build
docker build -t rchess-server .

# Run
docker run -d \
  --name rchess \
  -p 9001:9001 \
  -p 9002:9002 \
  -v rchess_data:/app/rchess_data \
  -e RCHESS_PUBLIC_HOST=chess.example.com \
  rchess-server

# With password
docker run -d \
  --name rchess \
  -p 9001:9001 \
  -p 9002:9002 \
  -v rchess_data:/app/rchess_data \
  rchess-server \
    --public chess.example.com \
    --apw mysecretadminpass \
    --name "My Chess Server" \
    --motd "Welcome! Games last 120min after disconnect."
```

### Option 4: Fly.io (free tier works)

```bash
fly launch   # follow prompts, use fly.toml
fly deploy
fly secrets set RCHESS_PUBLIC_HOST=myapp.fly.dev
```

The included `fly.toml` is pre-configured for ports 9001 + 9002.

### Option 5: Systemd (production Linux)

```ini
# /etc/systemd/system/rchess.service
[Unit]
Description=RChess Relay Server
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=rchess
WorkingDirectory=/opt/rchess
ExecStart=/opt/rchess/rchess-server \
    --public chess.example.com \
    --port 9001 \
    --admin 9002 \
    --data /var/lib/rchess \
    --apw changeme \
    --name "My Chess Server"
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

```bash
sudo systemctl enable --now rchess
sudo journalctl -u rchess -f
```

